            <ArticleTitle>Cranial neuralgias and headaches associated with cranial vascular disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1079-93, vi</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article discusses various cranial neuralgias and headaches linked to vascular disorders, including trigeminal neuralgia, intracerebral hemorrhage, temporal arteritis, and central nervous system angiitis. Also discussed are diagnostic methods, treatment options, and pain management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
